        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;arenson9&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"arenson9\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"LordLele\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/90ced4/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> LordLele:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I prefer text-based cards, however some icons to identify START and END turn action will be useful.</p>\n<p>I’ve translated the game in italian, and put the card with it’s translation inside card sleeves.<br>\nIn the translated text, I’ve used a different color marker to identify some keywords like POWER (violet), START of the turn (green), END of the turn (red).</p>\n<p>It’s useful mainly for villain and environment cards.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>red/green is a tough combo for folks who are color blind.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Uhm… you’re right.</p>\n<p>Maybe a icons/color combination?<br>\nLike a “green play” icon for “start of the turn” and a “red stop” icon for “end of the turn”…</p>",
